# Rules

Follow Xcode default code styling:
- Indentation: 4 spaces (Xcode default).
- Naming Conventions: PascalCase for types/structs/classes, camelCase for variables/functions.
- Typography / UI: Use native macOS system fonts and sizing (macOS Dynamic Type & system SF Pro / SF Mono, such as `.largeTitle`, `.title`, `.headline`, `.body`, `.subheadline`, `.caption`).
- Toolbar & Sidebar: Use native macOS components (`ToolbarItem`, `ToolbarItemGroup`, `.pickerStyle(.segmented)`, `.searchable`) and DO NOT ALTER the approved toolbar & sidebar design structure.
- SwiftUI: Use `@State private var` for local view state; avoid force unwrapping (`!`).
- Concurrency: Use modern Swift `async`/`await`.
- Unit Testing: Use the Swift Testing framework (`import Testing`).
